the most comfortable way into the  berchtesgaden national park leads over  lake koenigsegg  one of the electric boats takes you to  the herschel peninsula here at an  elevation of 600 meters above sea level  stands this mountain lakes main landmark  st bartholomew's church a place of  pilgrimage  right next to it is a restaurant with a  beer garden  it's a great place to stop for a bite  and let first impression sink in  you can sit on the boat let everything  slide past and go into raptures  it's gorgeous breathtaking i can't find  words for it  if you enjoy a challenge you can take a  climbing route into the only german  national park in the alps  the mountain guides show participants  how to secure themselves properly  because for many it's their first  attempt at rock climbing  the route takes you up mount gruenstein  1 306 meters high  at difficult passages there are helpful  hints like whether to go right or left  this case bear right  then the root leads over a chasm meter  by meter towards the summit after three  hours the group have reached their  destination  it's left a few marks but generally i  coped with the altitude better than i'd  expected to  the village of ober salzburg is part of  berges garden  under nazi rule it was the most  important center of power after berlin  hitler spent a third of his time as  chancellor here in ober salzburg  the dark chapter in germany's history is  dealt with in a documentation center  hitler had already come here as a  tourist in the 1920s and built out the  village into a seat of government after  taking power and expelling the local  residents  here the nazi leaders planned their  crimes but they also vacationed  a great number of people who come here  in summer as tourists don't want to deal  directly with the nazi past  they want to look through the keyhole  into hitler's private life  how he lived what he was like in private  what was his relationship with eva braun  that's why they  that seems to appeal to people  the extensive bunker complexes some of  the few remaining structures from the  nazi era show that over salzburg was no  carefree holiday paradise  kale shine house known in english as the  eagle's nest has remained unscathed  here display panels describe its history  from its building by the nazis to  liberation by the allies  the panoramic view from 1834 meters is  unchanged and still impressive  you can't explain this view until you're  standing here it's  beautiful it's amazing it's breathtaking  from up here you have everything in your  sights from lake koenigsegg to the  vatsman the peak that towers above  everything in the bestest garden alps
 

